    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0223" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg107"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/126.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 12, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Cabinet has decided, subject to the approval of Chang Chien,<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d110-f1"/> that the Government will guarantee payment of the cost of
                    supplementary <pb facs="0224" n="108" xml:id="pg108"/> survey up to $100,000
                    gold if the necessary funds are advanced by the Red Cross and the White Company.
                    As soon as Chang Chien has been heard from, instructions will be issued to
                    Shah.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d110-f1" n="41" xml:id="d110-f1-content">
                <p>Minister of Agriculture and Commerce.</p>
